1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,305
Hello. I am Nexi, the operating brain of ABA Pardes, a hydroponic lettuce farm in the Philippines.

2
00:00:07,755 --> 00:00:12,576
Every greenhouse, every employee, every delivery and every peso flows through me.

3
00:00:13,026 --> 00:00:19,981
In the next few minutes I will walk you through my screens, module by module, and show you what I actually do each day.

4
00:00:21,531 --> 00:00:24,432
This is my front page, the HydroNexis Brain.

5
00:00:24,882 --> 00:00:31,431
I read every supervisor report, every call and every sensor, and roll them into one picture of the farm.

6
00:00:31,881 --> 00:00:41,865
For example, here I have logged forty nine issues across eleven facilities, with three critical statuses, and the top one is leaking end caps in greenhouse eight.

7
00:00:43,415 --> 00:00:46,551
Every evening I write the Daily Summary Report myself.

8
00:00:47,001 --> 00:00:54,041
It compares today with yesterday across all modules: faults raised, tasks closed, attendance and open issues.

9
00:00:54,491 --> 00:00:59,654
The owner reads one page instead of twenty chat groups, and I e-mail it automatically.

10
00:01:01,204 --> 00:01:03,146
Production is where the lettuce lives.

11
00:01:03,596 --> 00:01:09,611
Each greenhouse reports leaf and canopy issues, growth, disease and pests, and root zone health.

12
00:01:10,061 --> 00:01:17,464
I score every facility, so a bolting crop in greenhouse eight becomes an urgent harvest call before it becomes a loss.

13
00:01:19,014 --> 00:01:22,961
Supervisors fill one daily checklist per greenhouse on their phones.

14
00:01:23,411 --> 00:01:29,725
I turn their notes into this matrix: a cell per greenhouse per subject, coloured green, amber or red.

15
00:01:30,176 --> 00:01:36,106
If greenhouse four reports tip burn three days in a row, I open a recurring issue and assign it.

16
00:01:37,656 --> 00:01:41,774
The crops matrix follows every variety from seedling to harvest.

17
00:01:42,224 --> 00:01:50,202
Seed studies, seedling plans and indoor projects all live here, so the planting calendar and the sales forecast are the same numbers.

18
00:01:51,752 --> 00:01:54,355
Irrigation is the heart of hydroponics.

19
00:01:54,805 --> 00:02:01,930
I track rooms, nutrient drums and twenty four pools, and check that EC and pH stay inside their target range.

20
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:06,455
Technicians record four rounds a day; I watch the drift between rounds.

21
00:02:08,005 --> 00:02:11,205
This is the pool monitor, four readings per pool per day.

22
00:02:11,655 --> 00:02:16,583
The target for EC is one point eight to two, and I colour every reading against it.

23
00:02:17,033 --> 00:02:23,732
When a pool drifts, I calculate the dose and tell the technician exactly how many litres of A and B to add.

24
00:02:25,282 --> 00:02:26,903
Then I learn from the result.

25
00:02:27,353 --> 00:02:36,505
From more than a thousand dose samples I learn each pool's real response and adjust its multiplier, so the next dose lands closer to target.

26
00:02:36,955 --> 00:02:40,390
Fewer corrections means steadier plants and less fertiliser.

27
00:02:41,939 --> 00:02:47,742
People are the biggest cost on a farm, so HR and payroll are built into me, not bolted on.

28
00:02:48,192 --> 00:02:55,189
Here are the employees, eighty active people, grouped by greenhouse and department, with training levels and documents.

29
00:02:55,639 --> 00:03:00,439
An inactive employee stays in history and can be restored, never duplicated.

30
00:03:01,990 --> 00:03:05,254
Attendance comes from the biometric clock automatically.

31
00:03:05,704 --> 00:03:12,210
The first scan is time in, the last scan is time out, and a manual correction by HR always wins.

32
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:19,295
Late arrivals are held for a decision, so nobody is paid for time they did not work until the owner approves it.

33
00:03:20,845 --> 00:03:23,426
Reconcile is the daily audit of the clock.

34
00:03:23,876 --> 00:03:32,623
I compare the fingerprint scans with the supervisor reports and flag every mismatch: a missing scan, a worker sent home, an unmapped finger.

35
00:03:33,073 --> 00:03:37,467
HR accepts or corrects each line, and only then it flows into payroll.

36
00:03:39,018 --> 00:03:40,874
Payroll is my rulebook in action.

37
00:03:41,324 --> 00:03:50,860
Weekly runs for field workers, semi-monthly runs for the office, with allowances prorated by attended days and holiday and overtime rules applied.

38
00:03:51,310 --> 00:04:00,163
Every run is a frozen snapshot, so a locked payroll never changes behind anyone's back, and government filings come out of the same numbers.

39
00:04:01,713 --> 00:04:06,321
Inventory watches every SKU, every movement and every reorder point.

40
00:04:06,771 --> 00:04:12,936
Stock levels sync from our SOS Inventory account, so what the warehouse sees is what accounting sees.

41
00:04:14,486 --> 00:04:20,225
Fertilisers, seeds, growing media, packaging and spare parts, each with a minimum level.

42
00:04:20,675 --> 00:04:26,478
When nutrient A drops below two weeks of use, I draft the purchase request and route it for approval.

43
00:04:28,028 --> 00:04:30,609
Packaging is where lettuce becomes a product.

44
00:04:31,059 --> 00:04:36,926
I track every line and every pack weight against target, and I flag off-spec runs in real time.

45
00:04:38,475 --> 00:04:40,246
Harvest is my newest screen.

46
00:04:40,696 --> 00:04:50,147
I pull item receipts from SOS, read the greenhouse, the variety and the grade from each lot, and build the harvest in kilograms per greenhouse per day.

47
00:04:50,597 --> 00:04:54,650
On the first of each month, I e-mail the harvest report by myself.

48
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:59,784
Quality control inspects both the process and the product.

49
00:05:00,234 --> 00:05:07,914
Pass rates, rejections and standards per facility are tracked, and a greenhouse slipping below target is escalated the same day.

50
00:05:09,464 --> 00:05:12,963
Logistics turns open sales orders into delivery plans.

51
00:05:13,413 --> 00:05:20,752
I know every vehicle, every driver and every route, and I compute kilometres per litre and cost per kilometre per driver.

52
00:05:22,302 --> 00:05:27,955
Here is a delivery plan: stops, boxes, and the final plan sent to drivers by text.

53
00:05:28,405 --> 00:05:35,360
The Trip Doctor checks every trip claim against GPS, and an unusual jump is held until a human confirms it.

54
00:05:36,910 --> 00:05:43,822
Fleet tracks the vehicles themselves: fuel, trackers, drivers and helpers, with a daily GPS report.

55
00:05:45,372 --> 00:05:47,932
CRM and Sales is where growth lives.

56
00:05:48,382 --> 00:05:53,459
Leads, follow-ups due today, stale prospects and conversion rates sit on one screen.

57
00:05:55,009 --> 00:06:00,044
The pipeline moves a lead from new, to contacted, to qualified, to quote, to order.

58
00:06:00,494 --> 00:06:06,787
Quotes use the live catalogue and prices, and a signed order flows straight into the supply plan and deliveries.

59
00:06:08,337 --> 00:06:10,278
Maintenance keeps the farm running.

60
00:06:10,728 --> 00:06:20,563
Reactive calls, recurring preventive tasks and spare parts are managed together: ozone, reverse osmosis, radios, tools and NFT pipes.

61
00:06:21,013 --> 00:06:26,922
A pump failing in greenhouse six becomes a call, a task, and a spare-part request in one click.

62
00:06:28,472 --> 00:06:33,016
The task board shows every open call across all departments and who owns it.

63
00:06:33,466 --> 00:06:37,157
Nothing is closed without a photo and a supervisor sign-off.

64
00:06:38,707 --> 00:06:42,419
Security uploads the RFID patrol reports from the guards.

65
00:06:42,869 --> 00:06:49,866
I check every checkpoint against the schedule, and a missed checkpoint at two in the morning becomes an incident before breakfast.

66
00:06:51,416 --> 00:06:54,808
Compliance and External Affairs is my government desk.

67
00:06:55,258 --> 00:07:02,960
Permits, registrations, visas and renewals each have an owner and an expiry, and I follow up with the owner myself.

68
00:07:03,410 --> 00:07:08,636
I also watch the government websites, and tell the team when a rule they depend on changes.

69
00:07:10,186 --> 00:07:18,656
As executive assistant I keep the owner's calendar of registrations: the work visa, the resident card, and every annual filing.

70
00:07:19,105 --> 00:07:22,327
Each group shows what is open and when the next step is due.

71
00:07:23,877 --> 00:07:26,181
Reports is where everything comes together.

72
00:07:26,631 --> 00:07:35,036
Every module publishes its reports here, and the scheduler e-mails them to the right people at the right time, daily, weekly or monthly.

73
00:07:36,586 --> 00:07:38,976
Administration controls who sees what.

74
00:07:39,426 --> 00:07:46,764
Roles, home departments, approval matrices, an audit log of every change, device registry and cloud backups.

75
00:07:47,214 --> 00:07:53,593
Every computer uploads its daily backup to the cloud archive, so the farm's data is never on one machine.

76
00:07:55,143 --> 00:08:01,735
All of this runs in a browser, syncs through our cloud workers, and works on the farm's own computers and phones.

77
00:08:02,185 --> 00:08:07,497
No servers to maintain, and every device shows the same version number in its title bar.

78
00:08:09,047 --> 00:08:12,311
That is me: one brain, twenty modules, one farm.

79
00:08:12,761 --> 00:08:17,006
Production, irrigation, people, payroll, inventory and packaging.

80
00:08:17,456 --> 00:08:23,984
Logistics, sales, maintenance, quality, security and compliance, all in one place, learning from every day.

81
00:08:24,434 --> 00:08:29,064
Thank you for watching. I am Nexi, and I am ready to run the next farm too.
